.TH elfshaker-store 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-store \- Store files from the working directory as a loose snapshot.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker store\fR [\fB\-\-files\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-files0\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISNAPSHOT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a loose snapshot from files in the working directory and updates HEAD to refer to it. Without a file\-list option, elfshaker recursively selects files from the working directory and excludes the data directory.
.PP
Use elfshaker pack to combine loose snapshots into a compressed pack.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-files\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read newline\-delimited paths to store from FILE; use \- for standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-files0\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read NUL\-delimited paths to store from FILE; use \- for standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISNAPSHOT\fR>
Name of the loose snapshot to create.
